::ALG2_U05_L08_GP_Q01::
Question ID: ALG2_U05_L08_GP_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.SYS.1; MLA.A2.SYS.2
Question:
Solve the system y=x+2 and y=6.
{
= x=4#Correct. Substitute y=6 into 6=x+2.
~ x=2#This uses the intercept only.
~ x=6#This is the y-value, not x.
~ x=8#This adds instead of subtracting.
}

::ALG2_U05_L08_GP_Q02::
Question ID: ALG2_U05_L08_GP_Q02
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.FN.4; MLA.A2.FN.5; MLA.A2.FN.6
Question:
How does y=(x-3)^2 transform y=x^2?
{
~ Left 3#The sign inside parentheses is interpreted oppositely.
= Right 3#Correct. x-3 shifts the graph right 3 units.
~ Up 3#There is no outside +3.
~ Down 3#There is no outside -3.
}

::ALG2_U05_L08_GP_Q03::
Question ID: ALG2_U05_L08_GP_Q03
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.FN.7; MLA.A2.FN.8
Question:
If f(x)=x+1 and g(x)=4x, what is f(g(2))?
{
~ 8#This stops after g(2).
~ 7#This applies functions in the wrong way.
= 9#Correct. g(2)=8 and f(8)=9.
~ 12#This multiplies after adding.
}

::ALG2_U05_L08_GP_Q04::
Question ID: ALG2_U05_L08_GP_Q04
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.FN.9; MLA.A2.FN.10
Question:
Find the inverse of f(x)=x-5.
{
~ f^-1(x)=x-5#This repeats the original.
~ f^-1(x)=5x#This does not undo subtracting 5.
~ f^-1(x)=1/(x-5)#Inverse notation is not reciprocal.
= f^-1(x)=x+5#Correct. Add 5 to undo subtracting 5.
}

::ALG2_U05_L08_GP_Q05::
Question ID: ALG2_U05_L08_GP_Q05
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.FN.3; MLA.A2.FN.11; MLA.A2.FN.12
Question:
Which solution is viable if a time model gives t=-4 and t=9?
{
= t=9 only#Correct. Negative time is not viable.
~ t=-4 only#Negative time is not viable.
~ Both values#One value violates the context.
~ Neither value#The positive time is viable.
}

